It would seem to me that a multi-player nethack game would need to
address a number of points:

	o The old nethack interface would have to be thrown out the
window.  One move, one clock tick is totally unacceptable for any
multi player game of reasonable size.

	o I would propose re-writing nethack in the xtrek mode:  an
open dungeon with continuous movement.  In fact, the final product
would neccessarily look something like the "gauntlet" video game; with
a little more character to each player/monster/items.

Yeah, I know no one cares, but people have been whining for
multi-player nethack for years now, so I'd just like to point out 
1) No one is going to write the damn thing, and
2) It will look nothing like the nethack you know and love.

